<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borna, Duke of Croatia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 821</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Borna was duke of the Dalmatian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> in the early 9th century and the first Croatian ruler recorded in contemporary sources, the Frankish royal annals. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>, he fought for Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ljudevit-posavski">Ljudevit Posavski</a>, the rebel duke of Pannonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, from 819 until his death in 821.</p></div>
